.TH codata 1 "28 November 2026" "2.7.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
codata \- get the fundamental physical constants


.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codata 
[\fIOPTION\fP]\.\.\.



.SH DESCRIPTION
.B codata
is a command line interface which prints all the CODATA constants.
.PP
The current values are from 2022.
Older values can be retrieved if needed and
the output can be filtered with \fIREGEX PATTERNS\fP.



.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-y, \-\-year " YEAR
CODATA constants: 2022, 2018, 2014, 2010
.TP
.BI "\-p, \-\-pattern " PATTERN
Regex pattern for filtering the constants. Multiple patterns can be 
passed by repeating this option.
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-value
Show only the value.
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-error
Show only the uncertainty.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-usage
Show usage text and exit.
.TP
.B
\-v, \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help text and exit.



.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
Minimal example
.nf
.ft CR
     codata
     codata -p Faraday
     codata -y 2014 -p molar.*gas,electron.*eV
     codata [B,b]oltzmann.*eV
.ft R
.fi

